# Downloaded AI model weights (ArcFace/buffalo_*, YOLO). Fetched on first use,
# hundreds of MB, and reproducible -- never belongs in the repo.
#
# ANCHORED with a leading slash, and this matters a great deal. A bare
# `models/` has no slash inside it, so git applies it at EVERY depth -- which
# silently excluded `backend/app/models/`, the twelve SQLAlchemy ORM modules
# (user, exam, attempt, question, proctor_event, ...) that define every table
# in this application. The first commit would have looked completely normal
# and produced a repository that cannot import `app.main`, with `git status`
# reporting nothing wrong because ignored files are not reported as missing.
#
# The two directories genuinely are unrelated despite the shared name:
# `backend/app/models/` is source, `backend/models/` is a weights cache. See
# the naming note in CODEBASE_REVIEW.md.
/backend/models/
*.onnx
*.pt

# Runtime uploads and generated files
uploads/
backend/uploads/
backend/.mpl-cache/
*.log
*.pid

# Local databases and data dumps
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.dump
*.sql

# Node/frontend dependencies and build output
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.cache/
.parcel-cache/
.vite/
# Vite rewrites its config to a temp .mjs beside the original on every dev-server
# start and leaves them behind; three are sitting in frontend/ right now. They
# are regenerated per run and meaningless to anyone else.
vite.config.js.timestamp-*
vite.config.ts.timestamp-*

